Hi all, I just ascended a rogue in NAO as an aleax and observed some
strange behavior. I was looking for theansweredrm to poly into when
wielding a mega weapon. (in my case grayswandir). In the olden days,
i would have picked a marlith, but now the best you can do is 2
weapon strikes with any character, so the choices were narrowed to
orc captain, elf king, dwarf king or aleax. 

After some thought, i thought even though the aleax doesn't get the
best weapon bonus it had a decent A.C. and i thought the extra kick
was cute. I was expecting that getting two hits with a grayswinder at
+7 was better than two weaponing it with a silver saber at +6 but it
didn't quite turn out that way. 

My first surprise came when i two weaponed in this new form. I was
under the impression that that can be done only in your natural form,
but tried it out anyways just for kicks. It turns out that an aleax
can indeed two weapon. I was surprised but i was going to test it
before i decided i found "the way" to play. 

The dev team usually thinks of everything, so i wanted to see what
exactly was going on. First, i had to find out if i got 4 strikes or
not. I took some time before a decent critter came my way, but i did
indeed get 4 strikes and a kick. Cool. Then i played further to see
what was hitting when. A vampire lord finally showed me that it went
grayswinder, silver saber, grayswinder, silver saber kick. Ok, got
it. 

At this point i was thinking, cool, i am in a form that will do double
the damage that i would do in natural form plus a little extra (for
the kick) but even though i put on boots of kicking and enchanted
them to +5 it wasn't the case that i was doing double damage. I did
more damage but it was not double. I killed a mess of critters to
test this but after awhile it was clear that on average (when silver
damage was not in effect) i was doing maybe 10 or 20 hp more than
normal, but not double. I don't know why.


Another thing i noticed may have been a fluke, but i never killed
anything with my last kick. Things died on my last saber strike, or
they lived until the my next attack, but they never died with my
kick. I didn't play the whole game in this form but i still thought i
played long enough for at least one creature to die from a boot to
the head but it was not to be. I started thinking that i was not
doing any damage with my kick. I don't know why. 

I also tested using the #kick command with unenchanted boots of
kicking. I used some wimpy critter with 11 hp. (a imp, qausit or
tengu) My barehanded skill was advanced to expert. I only did 2
points of damage. I don't know why, but i this point i started to
suspect that even if an Aleax gets 18/00 for str, it only counts for
carrying purposes. This would explain why i didn't do double damage
for the weapon attacks. monsters don't get a str bonus for their
attacks. At least, that is what i think is happening. I could be way
off mark. 

I still have questions, but since my next two classes are going to be
ra an c i don't think i will get them answered for at least another
month. (i want to see what other forms use two weapons. I know Xorns
cannot.I tried it.)

The last question is if i can two weapon with an aleax if my natural
form cannot, but that will be easy to test with my next game. I will
inform the group what i find out. 

